WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.234
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:07.367
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.033
Well, guys, let's get into it.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:12.701
Last night was the
94th Annual Academy Awards.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:15.467
[ Cheers and applause,
laughter ]

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:19.267
America may be divided,
but it was kind of nice

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.467
for all of us to come together

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.901
and say "holy crap"
at the same time.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.334
Of course, I have to address
the big moment

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.801
that everyone's talking about,
and that is

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.868
Questlove winning
the Oscar for Best Documentary!

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:33.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:36.868
Yes! Yes!

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.634
Questlove!

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.534
The best.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:45.901
Quest told me he's not gonna
let it go to his head.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:48.100
Well, actually, his
assistant's assistant told me

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.267
I couldn't get in touch
with Questlove,

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:50.667
but he is going to be
on the show tonight.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.534
He's gonna be our guest
on the show, and we'll talk.

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:55.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Tonight. Bringing the Oscar.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.567
But, actually, something else
did happen on the show.

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:00.801
Do you guys remember a few years
ago when the Oscars

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:03.834
literally announced the wrong
winner for Best Picture?

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:06.167
It turns out that was
child's play.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.634
That meant -- No.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.701
Yeah, there was a pretty rough
moment during the show,

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.667
and I think you all know what
I'm talking about.

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:16.100
Everyone in the audience
looked shocked,

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.601
and for once,
it wasn't from the Botox.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.400
Seriously, you know it was
a strange awards show

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.434
when it ends with a statement
from the LAPD.

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.100
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:31.067
Yep, in just a split second,
the Oscars went from

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:34.400
Oscar de la Renta to
Oscar de la Hoya, you know?

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.667
Look, you move the award for
Best Film Editing

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:39.701
out of the main broadcast,

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:40.801
and all hell breaks lose.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:42.434
I've been saying this...

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:43.734
But let's focus on the positive.

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:45.934
I thought Amy Schumer,
Regina Hall, and Wanda Sykes

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.701
did a great job
hosting the show.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:48.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.567
They did so well,
they are already rehearsing

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.667
their nos for when they are
asked to come back.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:58.801
Yeah, it's great.

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.667
It's a tough job
hosting the Oscars.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.934
It's a lot like drinking
Hard Mountain Dew.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.434
At first,
you can't wait to try it,

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:05.801
and then, after, you're like,
"Never again."

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.367
You know?

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.100
But on the bright side,
the Oscars rebounded from

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.767
last year's record-low ratings,

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.467
drawing over 15 million viewers.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.067
That is like taking all
the people who watched

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:20.133
the Best Picture nominees
and adding 15 million viewers.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.501
There were a lot of reasons
more people watched this year,

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:24.634
and I think one of them
might have been

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:26.133
Timothée Chalamet outfit.

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.133
Take a look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:29.601
Yeah.

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:34.467
Yep, it turns out Chalamet
is French for "chest wax."

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:36.000
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.000
Vladimir Putin calls that look
"business casual."

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.000
But let's switch gears.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.901
During a speech in Poland
this weekend,

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.634
President Biden went off script

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.434
and said that Putin
cannot remain in power.

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:53.334
However, The White House
quickly walked it back

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:56.467
and said Biden wasn't
calling for his removal.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:57.667
That's like if
Reagan's staff said,

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:58.868
"He actually meant to say,

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.767
'Mr. Gorbachev,
tear down this wallpaper.'"

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:05.067
Meanwhile, I heard that,
this week,

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:08.767
the House is expected to pass
a bill legalizing marijuana.

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:11.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:13.767
This bill probably
won't pass right away.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:15.234
Experts are saying that
they will most likely

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:17.167
puff, puff, then pass.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:21.133
That one guy really got it.
-Nice!

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.634
-One guy really got it.
-Yeah, really got it.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:27.300
-He almost got it too soon.
He was like, "Ah-ha-ha!"

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.300
That's right -- the bill will be
signed at The White House,

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.701
then framed at White Castle.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:32.167
That's interesting.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:34.734
And, finally,
a woman in the U.K.

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:36.267
just broke the world record
for the most

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:39.367
chicken nuggets
eaten in one minute.

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:41.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.267
And she did it after
telling her boyfriend,

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:45.300
"I don't want my own.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.567
I'll just eat a few of yours."

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:47.601
We have a great show.

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:49.834
Give it up for The Roots,
everybody!

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:11.100
It is Monday.
We are excited to be back.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.367
We have a great, great
week of shows ahead.

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:17.267
Jared Leto will be here.
Sienna Miller will be here.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:18.968
Hugh Jackman will be joining us.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:22.000
And we have --
I know -- we love Hugh Jackman.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.667
And we have a music performance
from Red Hot Chili Peppers.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:26.834
This is a big week.
-Whoa!

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:29.501
-But, first, what a show
we have for you tonight.

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:32.801
He is the host of "Last Week
Tonight with John Oliver,"

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:35.868
which airs Sundays at
11:00 p.m. on HBO.

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:38.167
John Oliver is here tonight!

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.067
Super-funny.

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:44.934
Plus, she's one of
our favorites.

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:46.934
She stars in
the new film "Moonshot,"

00:04:46.934 --> 00:04:49.534
which begins streaming
this Thursday on HBO Max.

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:51.567
Lana Condor is here!

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:58.934
Plus, he just won an
Academy Award last night

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:01.133
for his documentary,
"Summer of Soul."

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.767
We're talking to
Questlove from The Roots.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:06.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:09.767
And we got music from
Buddy featuring Blxst tonight.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.834
-Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:18.534
I loved the Academy Awards
last night.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:21.501
I mean, despite that incident.

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:24.334
I loved seeing awards shows.

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:25.400
It makes me happy.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.934
My mom would be really
into award shows,

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:29.868
any award show -- Emmys, Oscars.

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:32.901
My mom would dress up in a
dress, like, in a gown kind of.

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:33.901
-Aww.

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:35.801
-Yeah. And we'd have champagne,

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:37.834
if it was, like, cheap
champagne, whatever it was.

00:05:37.834 --> 00:05:40.334
She would, like,
have a speech ready to go.

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:41.834
Like, we loved watching it.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:44.100
And that's -- It was like,
"Oh, they have hosts again."

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:47.133
It was so -- a step back
to normalcy, you know?

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:49.634
And I loved the opening
with Beyoncé

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.701
and just Beyoncé looking
awesome, as always,

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:54.067
and that smile
like she can only do.

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:55.934
Like, she just --
She knows how to do it.

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:58.667
And then I thought the hosts
did a great job.

00:05:58.667 --> 00:06:01.434
And then the Will-Chris thing,

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:03.400
I was just bummed, disturbed.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.734
I wish it didn't happen.

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:08.033
But it didn't stop me
from just loving the business

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.100
and what we do.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.767
We chose to do this, you know?

00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:13.968
And to get to see everybody
and people that are on our show

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:16.234
and give out, you know, like,

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:17.601
editing, cinematography --
anything.

00:06:17.601 --> 00:06:20.200
Just looking at
and celebrating this business.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.834
I thought it was awesome,
and no way could you even

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:25.834
think that your friend
was going to be up for

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:28.467
an Academy Award and win.

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:31.033
And Questlove --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:33.534
I was screaming!
-Yeah.

00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:36.167
-I was crying.
I was like, "Ahhh!"

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:38.234
I'm, like, texting him,
"Oh, my God!"

00:06:38.234 --> 00:06:39.567
You know? Like...

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:41.000
Of course, he wasn't going to
deal with a text from me,

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.701
but I was just freaking out,
just so happy for him.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:46.133
This guy worked
so hard on this thing,

00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:48.934
and just -- It's an Oscars
that I'll never forget.

00:06:48.934 --> 00:06:50.834
It was awesome.
So, congrats again to Questlove.

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:52.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:54.133
And everyone behind the Oscars.
It was a good show.

